From 1c1db603b50c7739b48c37f6b69ddd9a874c5893 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 02:42:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 406/406] Part, Unified: the overlaps measured in the
 background stop when the application quits

A night of GUI runs under ASan: after the documents were closed and the
window too, a design check still measuring overlaps in its threads ran
on into the torn-down OCC (SEGV in a boolean, exit code 1 after a normal
close; the field test's unexplained exit code 1). Part.cancelInterferences
stops the runs at their next pair; on aboutToQuit the design check stops
its threads and waits for them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
